# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Competition data. NEVER commit any of this.
#
# This competition licenses its data for challenge use only -- some hosts
# explicitly forbid uploading it to public repositories and mention legal
# action. Derived artefacts (preprocessed caches, embeddings, extracted
# features, OOF predictions, trained weights) are still competition data.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

# Raw data directories
data/
runtime/
/smoke/

# Preprocessed caches and derived arrays (train_*.npz etc. are up to 4.5 GB)
*.npz
*.npy
*.parquet
*.nii.gz
research/cache/

# Trained model weights (derived from competition data)
*.pt
*.pth
*.ckpt
*.safetensors
model/
model_*/
submission_model/model/

# Feature tables and label exports (these carry competition labels)
research/*.csv

# Submissions
submission/*.zip
submission/*.csv
staging/*.csv

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Environments, caches, tooling
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
.venv/
**/__pycache__/
*.pyc
.ipynb_checkpoints/
.gstack/
*.log

# CatBoost writes training artifacts next to the run; never source.
catboost_info/

# Claude Code worktrees: live git worktrees, never part of this repo
.claude/worktrees/

# Release weights: built by scripts/export_weights.py; Nhat decides how they are published.
release/weights/
release/*.csv
release/*.tar
